guttormsen ueland nesthus nygard schneede vollset refsum hyperhomocysteinemia micromol hordaland jci119024 hoogeveen kostense beks mackaay jakobs bouter heine stehouwer hyperhomocysteinemia atv israelsson brattstrom hultberg izumi iwai ohmichi shimoike methylenetetrahydrofolate swendseid selhub bostom fortification nejm199905133401901 passen ruggie sora thermolabile methylenetetrahydrofolate norusis messer homocyst ine jci112461 susmano sora norusis ruggie thermolabile methylenetetrahydrofolate kluijtmans kastelein lindemans heil bruschke jukema trijbels boerma thermolabile methylenetetrahydrofolate kluijtmans frosst oost heijer trijbels rozen hyperhomocysteinemia methylenetetrahydrofolate lindenbaum stabler cobalamin loehrer haefeli adenosylmethionine methyltetrahydrofolate atv lolin masarei hyperhomocysteinaemia malinow bostom homocyst ine malinow ducimetiere luc arveiler cambien upson homocyst ine malinow duell phillipson gluckman upson homocyst ine cereal fortified nejm199804093381501 malinow duell gluckman holzgang seltzer multivitamin methylenetetrahydrofolate atv matsushita muramatsu methylenetetrahydrofolate moghadasian homocyst ine montalescot ankri chadefaux vekemans blacher drobinski benzidia kamoun s0167 kurihara hamada kurihara shindo hashi yazaki atv taguchi kurihara kitaoka kaneda kurihara maemura shindo minamino methylenetetrahydrofolate mthfr schaubel desmeules wigle mudd skovby pettigrew wilcken pyeritz andria bromberg cerone homocystinuria cystathionine chutorian wexman grieco heininger glassman gaull feit wexman naurath riezler stabler lindenbaum nygard nordrehaug refsum ueland farstad vollset nejm199707243370403 nygard refsum ueland vollset hordaland olszewski szostak omenn beresford motulsky yamakawa arinami amemiya kawata sugishita methylenetetrahydrofolate s0021 pancharuniti sauberlich macaluso acton homocyst ine homocyst inaemia hyperhomocysteinemia refsum ueland nygard vollset refsum ueland lipidol rimm colditz hennekens stampfer arheart refsum brattstrom ueland rubba meleady comac lente kottke savon selhub hyperhomocysteinemia pyridoxal schorah devitt lucock dowell ejcn siscovick malinow rosendaal beverly psaty longstreth koepsell raghunathan methylenetetrahydrofolate selhub homocysteinemia skovby homocysteinemia stampfer malinow newcomer upson ullmann tishler hennekens homocyst ine stehouwer weijenberg jakobs feskens kromhout atv moneta schuff s0741 thuillier chadefaux vekemans bonnefont aupetit rochette montalescot couty kamoun ankri 677c methylenetetrahydrofolate inherit mahnken selhub fortification ubbink fehily elwood vermaak caerphilly s0021 ubbink vermaak staden bissbort homocysteinemia angiographically bf01649290 ubbink vermaak merwe delport potgieter hyperhomocysteinemia ubbink merwe vermaak delport hyperhomocysteinemia bf00180030 hennekens stabler stampfer kluijtmans refsum ueland kruyssen 677c methylenetetrahydrofolate s0021 kruyssen schouten witteman grobbee ueland refsum atv stampfer buring gaziano stabler hennekens a008828 verhoeff kastelein methylenetetrahydrofolate s0021 mcpartlin mcnulty mcpartlin qjmed wilcken homocysteinemia homocystinuria wilcken mccredie methylenetetrahydrofolate mthfr c677t atv wilcken wilcken homocystinuria inherit wilcken wilcken jci108350 woodside yarnell mccrum gey hyperhomocysteinemia battista homocyst ine heijer spaans rosendaal haak wijermans atv bockxmeer mamotte vasikaran methylenetetrahydrofolate franken jakobs stehouwer rauwerda hyperhomocysteinemia eckardstein malinow upson schonfeld assmann hemostatic homocyst inemia atv','Abstract OBJECTIVE: To establish guidelines for the screening and treatment of hyperhomocysteinemia in the investigation and management of coronary artery disease (CAD). OPTIONS: Measurement of plasma total homocysteine (tHcy) levels in the fasting state or 4-6 hours after oral methionine load; vitamin supplementation with folic acid and vitamins B6 and B12; adherence to the recommended daily allowance of dietary sources of folate and vitamins B6 and B12. OUTCOMES: This article reviews the available evidence on the association between plasma tHcy levels and CAD and the effect of lowering tHcy levels through vitamin supplementation or dietary intake. EVIDENCE: MEDLINE was searched for relevant English-language articles published from January 1966 to June 1999; also reviewed were additional articles identified from the bibliographies. BENEFITS, HARMS AND COSTS: Cardiovascular disease is the leading cause of death in Canada. Homocysteine, generated in the metabolism of methionine, may have a role in the development of cardiovascular disease. The prevalence of hyperhomocysteinemia in the general population is between 5% and 10% and may be as high as 30%-40% in the elderly population. If population-based studies are correct, tHcy may be responsible for up to 10% of CAD events and thus may represent an important and potentially modifiable risk factor for cardiovascular disease. Laboratory testing for tHcy is currently restricted to research centres, and costs range from $30 to $50 per person. Newer, less costly techniques have been developed and should become readily available with time. VALUES: The strength of evidence was evaluated using the methods of the Canadian Task Force on Preventive Health Care. RECOMMENDATIONS: Although there is insufficient evidence to recommend the screening or management of hyperhomocysteinemia at present (grade C recommendation), adherence to recommended daily allowance of dietary sources of folate and vitamins B12 and B6 should be encouraged. If elevated tHcy levels are discovered, vitamin deficiency should be ruled out to allow specific treatment and prevention of complications, such as neurological sequelae due to vitamin B12 deficiency. Experts in the field advocate treatment of elevated tHcy levels in high-risk people, such as those with a personal or family history of premature atherosclerosis or a predisposition to develop hyperhomocysteinemia. Definitive guidelines for the management of hyperhomocysteinemia await the completion of randomized trials to establish the effect of vitamin supplementation on CAD events. VALIDATION: The findings of this analysis were reviewed through an iterative process by the members of the Canadian Task Force on Preventive Health Care. SPONSORS: The Canadian Task Force on Preventive Health Care is funded through a partnership between the Provincial and Territorial Ministries of Health and Health Canada. Full Text The Full Text of this article is available as a PDF (282.3 KB). Selected References These references are in PubMed. This may not be the complete list of references from this article. Alfthan G., Pekkanen J., Jauhiainen M., Pitkäniemi J., Karvonen M., Tuomilehto J., Salonen J. T., Ehnholm C. Relation of serum homocysteine and lipoprotein(a) concentrations to atherosclerotic disease in a prospective Finnish population based study. Atherosclerosis. 1994 Mar;106(1):9–19. doi: 10.1016/0021-9150(94)90078-7. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Anderson J. L., King G. J., Thomson M. J., Todd M., Bair T. L., Muhlestein J. B., Carlquist J. F. A mutation in the methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase gene is not associated with increased risk for coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction. J Am Coll Cardiol. 1997 Nov 1;30(5):1206–1211. doi: 10.1016/s0735-1097(97)00310-0. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Arnesen E., Refsum H., Bønaa K. H., Ueland P. M., Førde O. H., Nordrehaug J. E. Serum total homocysteine and coronary heart disease. Int J Epidemiol. 1995 Aug;24(4):704–709. doi: 10.1093/ije/24.4.704. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Aronow W. S., Ahn C. Association between plasma homocysteine and coronary artery disease in older persons. Am J Cardiol. 1997 Nov 1;80(9):1216–1218. doi: 10.1016/s0002-9149(97)00643-7. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Bostom A. G., Silbershatz H., Rosenberg I. H., Selhub J., D''Agostino R. B., Wolf P. A., Jacques P. F., Wilson P. W. Nonfasting pl