surgery and overall survival in the US military health system. JAMA Surg. 2019;154(3):e185113. doi: 10.1001/jamasurg.2018.5113. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Sheppard VA, Oppong BA, Hampton R, et al. Disparities in breast cancer surgery delay: the lingering effect of race. Ann Surg Oncol. 2015;22(9):2902–29011. doi: 10.1245/s10434-015-4397-3. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Walsh RL, Lofters A, Moineddin R, Kryzanowska M, Grunfeld E. Primary care continuity and wait times to receiving breast cancer chemotherapy: a population-based retrospective cohort study using CanIMPACT data. Curr Oncol. 2021;28:4786–4804. doi: 10.3390/curroncol28060405. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Valente S, Al-Hilli Z, Liu Y, Greve N, Tu C, Grobmyer SR. Association of patient factors with time to treatment for breast cancer. Breast J. 2020;26(10):1995–2001. doi: 10.1111/tbj.14046. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Kvasnovsky CL, Kesmodel AB, Gargasin JL, et al. Expansion of screening mammography in the Veterans Health Administration: implications for breast cancer treatment. JAMA Surg. 2013;148(11):999–1004. doi: 10.1001/jamasurg.2013.3738. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Casey JT, Berkowitz L, Cashy J, Wichramasinghe N, Schaeffer A, Gonzalez C. A protocol based, electronic medical record enabled care coordination system improves the timeliness and efficiency of care for patients with hematuria. J Urol. 2013;190(1):212–217. doi: 10.1016/j.juro.2013.01.018. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 31. Laws A, Crocker A, Dort J, et al. Improving wait times and patient experience through implementation of a provincial expedited diagnostic pathway for BI-RADS 5 breast lesions. Ann Surg Oncol. 2019;26(10):3361–3367. doi: 10.1245/s10434-019-07558-7. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Richards M, Anderson M, Carter P, et al. The impact of COVID-19 pandemic on cancer care. Nat Cancer. 2020;1:565–567. doi